An iterable is an object that can be iterated over.
Examples:
list
tuple
string
set
dictionary

Example without iterator:
numbers = [10, 20, 30]
for number in numbers:
    print(number)numbers = [10, 20, 30]
iterator = iter(numbers)
print(next(iterator))
print(next(iterator))
print(next(iterator))

Output:
10
20
30

Calling next() again:
print(next(iterator))

will produce:
StopIteration

Iterable vs Iterator
Iterable Can provide an iterator.
